course: dictionary
lesson: 9603
title: Stride: long steps and great progress
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Stride has two main jobs. As a verb, to stride means to walk with long, quick, confident steps. As a noun, a stride is one long step, or how far one step reaches. «Ostriches can run with strides of about 4 to 5 metres.» The numbers around the word are the clue: a stride is measured by its length.
explain: Stride can also show how a character feels. «He strode into the room» tells you he walked in boldly, not creeping. The long steps are the clue. If the sentence said he strode in and shouted at everyone, you would know he was angry.
explain: Stride also appears in phrases that have nothing to do with walking. «Make great strides» means to make good progress, to get better. A teacher might write, «you have made great strides in reading.» «Take it in your stride» means to deal with a problem calmly. Check the context: if the sentence is about getting better, the meaning is progress.
fact: To stride means to walk with long, quick, confident steps.
fact: A stride is one long step, or the length of a step.
fact: «Make great strides» means to make good progress.
fact: «Take it in your stride» means to deal with a problem calmly.
fact: In PE and running, athletes lengthen their stride to run faster.
exercise: In «Ostriches can run with strides of about 4 to 5 metres», what is a stride? | A bird that runs fast | *One long step, or the length of a step | To shout loudly | A sort of shoe
exercise: «He strode into the room.» What does strode tell you about him? | He fell over | He crept in quietly | *He walked in with long, confident steps | He ran out of the room
exercise: A teacher writes, «you have made great strides in reading.» What does this mean? | *You have made good progress and got better | You have walked a long way while reading | You have read a very stride-long book | You have stopped reading
test: Dan will take the test in his stride. What does this mean? | He will measure the test in strides | He will run away from the test | He will ask someone else to do it | *He will deal with it calmly
test: In «The giant bird strode about on all fours», which word is a verb? | bird | *strode | fours | giant
exam: Which phrase means to deal with a problem calmly? | *Take it in your stride | Make great strides | Strode into the room | Stride length
